[-] Expose the agent-native tool surface through Pi =pi-interface $In progress. Second Pi slice shipped: the project-local extension registers workspace_status (brief/full projection over the kernel status surface) and workspace_delta (checkpoint delta with optional --since) as native Pi tools that exec the kernel binary and return its JSON verbatim, adding no kernel semantics. Expected no-runtime conditions degrade to plain text; only failed kernel invocations throw. Validated by 8 TS tests, strict typecheck, 33 Rust tests, fmt, clippy, and a fresh pi -p session that oriented via the tools alone (objective, claim freshness, latest checkpoint) without shelling to the CLI. Read auto-capture residuals still visible: later-loaded context middleware can alter the read projection, outside-range concurrent edits can affect container fingerprints, and orientation tool results are not themselves observed. Next session: decide whether the loop verbs (observe/claim/transaction) deserve the same projection, or move to nvim-projection.$ !2 +integration ^2026-08-31T22:31 <kernel #01a05b73-6878-7920-bdd3-e8e37f37b4da
[ ] Project shared workspace state into Neovim =nvim-projection $Create a thin human projection using native quickfix, signs, commands, statusline data, and semantic jumps. The shared substrate is authoritative; Neovim remains the human cockpit rather than the daemon.$ !3 +integration ^2026-08-31T22:31 <pi-interface #01a05b73-6884-79b2-a3af-4577cc07e03a
[ ] Dogfood the MVP and decide the next architecture =dogfood $Run representative maintenance tasks, record context churn, stale-evidence incidents, recovery quality, validation gaps, and human-agent handoffs. Use evidence to choose persistence, adapter, and collaboration scope for the next charter.$ !2 +evaluation ^2026-08-31T22:31 <pi-interface #01a05b73-6890-7991-a687-bd1eff659924
[ ] Fix the edit-time hook that reformats Rust files non-canonically $An edit-time hook in the agent harness (not this repo — .githooks/pre-commit is check-only) reformats tests/walking_skeleton.rs into a non-rustfmt-canonical style between turns. Three incidents so far: run 5 (caught by cargo fmt --check) and run 7 (twice, identical 10-insertion/20-deletion diff each time, collapsing multi-line forms into chained one-liners). Impact is currently absorbed on three levels: git checkout restores the committed canonical form, the pre-commit fmt gate rejects it from commits, and since run 7 the rustfmt-normalized fingerprints keep observations and claims current through the byte drift. Fix at the source: configure or disable the harness edit-time formatter so it either runs rustfmt on .rs files or leaves them alone. Verify by editing a .rs test file and confirming the working tree stays clean between turns.$ !5 +environment ^2026-09-01T19:18 #01a05fe9-40b4-7880-b405-ce1fbc0d8820
